    <statement><p>Evaluate the following without a calculator.
Simplify your answers as much as possible.</p>
<p>(a) <m>\sqrt{ (-6)^2 } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>(-1)^{3} \cdot \sqrt{16} =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>(0.36)^{1/2} =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>(d) <m>(-64)^{2/3} =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>16</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> SOLUTION </alert>



(a) <m>\sqrt{ (-6)^2 } = \sqrt{36} = 6</m>.



(b) <m>(-1)^{3} \cdot \sqrt{16} = -1\sqrt{4^2} = -4</m>.



(c) <m>(0.36)^{1/2} = \left(\frac{36}{100}\right)^{1/2} = \frac{6}{10} = 0.6</m>.



(d) <m>(-64)^{2/3} = (-4)^2 = 16</m>.



</solution>
